<title>UK: Triplex Lloyd shareholders back Wm. Cook bid.</title>
<headline>Triplex Lloyd shareholders back Wm. Cook bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Triplex Lloyd Plc said on Monday its shareholders had approved its planned acquisition of steel firm William Cook Plc.</p>
<p>On Friday, William Cook reiterated its rejection of Triplex's hostile bid, adding that it expected to show a substantial profit rise for the year.</p>
<p>Triplex responded later that day by arguing that William Cook was exaggerating its potential.</p>
<p>Triplex's cash and share bid values Cook at about 309 pence per share.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
